    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n19273" root="سخو and سخى" body-key="s">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">سَخِىٌّ</span></b>  <i>Liberal, bountiful, munificent,</i> or <i>generous;</i> (S, * Msb, K;) as also ↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">سَاخٍ</span></b>  and ↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">سَخٍ</span></b> :
(Msb, TA:) fem. of the first with <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">ة</span>: pl. masc.
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أَسْخِيَآءُ</span> and <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">سُخَوَآءُ</span>: and pl. fem. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">سَخِيَّاتٌ</span> and
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">سَخَايَا</span>. (K.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  [Hence,] one says, <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">إِنَّهُ لَسَخِىُّ</span>
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">النَّفْسِ عَنْهُ</span> [<i>Verily he is content to leave,</i> or <i>relinquish, it</i>]. (TA.) ＝   
    <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer1"> </span>-A2-  See also 1, last sentence.

